title: Naresh_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite SportsAcademy>>

// Scene Setup - Sports academy visit
Drawn by curiosity about professional cricket facilities, Raju chooses to walk past the prestigious sports academy on his way home from school. He knows this place represents the pinnacle of cricket training.

The imposing walls of the sports academy loom before Raju. The sound of leather on willow echoes from within, drawing him closer. Naresh, the groundskeeper, watches from near the entrance.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Angry>>
Naresh: Oi! You there, boy! What are you doing lurking around here?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Irritated>>
Naresh: This is not a public playground for slum kids. Go play your street cricket in your own galli where you belong.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Anxious>>
Raju: I just wanted to watch for a moment, bhaiya. I won't disturb anyone.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Sad>>
Raju: I've never seen proper cricket nets before. I'm trying to learn how real cricket is played.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Serious>>
Naresh: Watch? Listen, boy, I have strict rules to follow here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Worried>>
Naresh: If Coach Sharma sees me letting unauthorized people onto the grounds, I'll lose this job faster than you can say 'cricket.'

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Serious>>
Naresh: This is my livelihood, not a charity for curious children.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Serious>>
Naresh: These facilities cost more money than your entire neighborhood sees in a year.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Serious>>
Naresh: The insurance alone would bankrupt me if something gets damaged. Now move along before you get both of us in trouble.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Serious>>
Raju: I understand, bhaiya. I don't want to cause you problems.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Determined>>
Raju: But one day, I'll play here too. Not as someone sneaking around, but as someone who belongs.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Skeptical>>
Naresh: Hmph. Big dreams for such a small boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Skeptical>>
Naresh: But dreams don't pay academy fees or buy proper equipment. Reality is harder than fantasy, child.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Confident>>
Raju: Maybe. But without dreams, there's no reason to work toward reality.

<<HideCharacter>>
As Raju walks away, he carries both disappointment and unexpected determination. The brief encounter has strengthened his resolve to find a way to overcome these obstacles.

<<set $Naresh_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: Naresh_Day2
tags: 
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite SportsAcademy>>

// Scene Setup - Day 2
Despite yesterday's dismissal, Raju returns to the academy at the same time. He positions himself at a respectful distance, hoping to watch without causing trouble.

The afternoon sun casts long shadows across the grounds. Naresh notices the young man's return with irritation and grudging recognition of his persistence.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Irritated>>
Naresh: You again? I thought I made myself clear yesterday.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Annoyed>>
Naresh: Don't you boys have anything better to do than hang around places where you don't belong?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: I can't stop thinking about cricket, bhaiya. Every night I try to practice what I saw yesterday.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Anxious>>
Raju: But I know I'm missing things. I just want to learn, even if I can only watch from out here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Serious>>
Raju: I won't cause any trouble or ask for anything. I promise.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Quizzical>>
Naresh: Hmph. I've worked here for ten years, watched hundreds of kids try to sneak in.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Quizzical>>
Naresh: Most fool around and break expensive equipment. But you... you just stand there with those big eyes.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Astonished>>
Naresh: You're staring at every single ball like your life depends on it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: Because I want to remember everything!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: The way their feet move before each shot, how they hold the bat differently for different deliveries.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: The way they position their bodies to generate power. I try to copy it all later when I practice at home.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Quizzical>>
Naresh: You're analyzing technique just by watching?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Astonished>>
Naresh: Most of the paying students inside can't remember basic instruction from one session to the next.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Quizzical>>
Naresh: But you're studying cricket like it's... like it's science.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: Cricket is science, isn't it? Every movement has a purpose, every technique solves a problem.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Confident>>
Raju: The students inside have coaches explaining everything. But I have to figure it out by watching.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Confident>>
Raju: Maybe that makes me see things differently.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Smiling>>
Naresh: Crazy kid. Standing out here in the heat just to watch cricket practice.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Smiling>>
Naresh: But maybe... maybe not completely useless. At least you're not throwing rocks at the equipment like the others.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Serious>>
Raju: I would never damage anything, bhaiya. This place is too precious.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Serious>>
Raju: Even watching from outside teaches me more about cricket than I could learn anywhere else.

<<HideCharacter>>
As the second day concludes, Naresh shows the first signs of softening. Raju's analytical approach has distinguished him from other unauthorized visitors.

<<set $Naresh_Day = 3>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: Naresh_Day3
