<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite SportsAcademy>>

// Scene Setup - Day 3
For the third day, Raju returns bringing a small notebook. He wants to demonstrate that his watching serves a genuine educational purpose.

The notebook tucked under his arm represents evidence of his serious approach. Naresh's skepticism has begun to crack.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Quizzical>>
Naresh: Back again, I see. And what's that you're carrying?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Skeptical>>
Naresh: Don't tell me you're planning to write complaints about being kept out.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: It's my cricket journal, bhaiya. I've been writing down everything I observe here.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Proud>>
Raju: Different techniques, how the students hold their bats, what the coach corrects them for.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: I study it every night and practice the movements at home.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Astonished>>
Naresh: You're... taking notes? On cricket technique?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Astonished>>
Naresh: By watching from outside the fence?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: Yesterday I saw a student struggling with his forward defensive shot.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Confident>>
Raju: The coach showed him three times how to position his front foot, but I could see the real problem.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: He wasn't transferring his weight properly. I've been practicing that weight transfer myself to understand why it matters.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Quizzical>>
Naresh: And did you figure it out? Why the weight transfer matters?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: Yes! Without proper weight transfer, you can't adjust quickly if the ball bounces differently.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Confident>>
Raju: The front foot position creates the foundation, but the weight shift creates the flexibility to respond.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: It's like... like building a house that can bend without breaking.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Astonished>>
Naresh: You learned that just from watching?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Overjoyed>>
Naresh: That's more cricket understanding than half my paying students develop after months of direct instruction.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Excited>>
Naresh: Show me this notebook. I want to see what you've been recording.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Astonished>>
Naresh: These drawings... these notes... beta, you've created your own cricket textbook.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Overjoyed>>
Naresh: Look at this analysis of different bowling grips and how they affect ball movement.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Proud>>
Naresh: Some of our advanced students couldn't explain this.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Excited>>
Raju: Cricket makes sense when you watch it carefully, bhaiya.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" Confident>>
Raju: Every technique solves a specific problem. I may not have access to coaching, but I can still learn if I pay attention.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Proud>>
Naresh: You know what, boy? In ten years of maintaining these grounds, I've never seen anyone study cricket with this kind of scientific approach.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Smiling>>
Naresh: Most kids just want to hit big shots and look impressive.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Serious>>
Naresh: How do you plan to build on this foundation you've created?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Naresh" Serious>>
Naresh: What's your next step in this cricket education?
<<AutoAdvance true>>
Make a Choice
